Subject: [PATCH] venus: feedback buffers in host-cached memory

Venus keeps the status of fences, timeline semaphores, events and queries
in feedback buffers: a command appended to a submission writes the status
on the host GPU, and the guest CPU reads it through its mapping of the
virtio-gpu hostmem BAR. The buffer went into the first HOST_COHERENT memory
type, which on NVIDIA is uncached system memory.

On an RTX 4060 Laptop host (Intel i7-13700H, NVIDIA 615.71.09) the host
GPU's writes to that type never became visible to the guest: the guest kept
reading the status it had written itself, from a CPU cache line the GPU
write did not invalidate (a clflush before the read showed the GPU's value
every time). Every fence and timeline semaphore wait hung, and
vn_get_fence_status reported "ffb must be signaled now". The cached
HOST_COHERENT type saw every write, as did device-local host-visible memory.

Prefer a HOST_COHERENT | HOST_CACHED type for feedback buffers, and fall
back to any HOST_COHERENT type. Polling cached memory is also cheaper.

Evidence: docs/nvfb.md, docs/evidence/nvfb/ (src/guest-fbtest/fbguest.c).
Origin: vmlab-win3d nvfb worker.
---
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_feedback.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_feedback.c
index 0f9ab82..f347291 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_feedback.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_feedback.c
@@ -71,9 +71,22 @@ vn_feedback_buffer_create(struct vn_device *dev,
    struct vn_buffer *buf = vn_buffer_from_handle(fb_buf->buf_handle);
    const VkMemoryRequirements *mem_req =
       &buf->requirements.memory.memoryRequirements;
-   const uint32_t mem_type_index =
-      vn_get_memory_type_index(mem_props, mem_req->memoryTypeBits,
-                               VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT);
+   /* Prefer a host-cached type. The guest CPU polls the feedback slots
+    * that the host GPU writes, and a host GPU may write uncached system
+    * memory without snooping the CPU caches: on an RTX 4060 Laptop host
+    * (Intel CPU) the guest kept reading a stale cache line of the uncached
+    * HOST_COHERENT type, so fences never signalled, while the cached type
+    * saw every write (docs/nvfb.md). Cached memory is also cheaper to poll.
+    */
+   uint32_t mem_type_index = vn_get_memory_type_index(
+      mem_props, mem_req->memoryTypeBits,
+      VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT |
+         VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT);
+   if (mem_type_index >= mem_props->memoryTypeCount) {
+      mem_type_index =
+         vn_get_memory_type_index(mem_props, mem_req->memoryTypeBits,
+                                  VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT);
+   }
    if (mem_type_index >= mem_props->memoryTypeCount) {
       result = VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED;
       goto out_destroy_buffer;
